+We present \mecc{}, the MoE Expert Cache Compiler, to connect these two stages. Compilation ranks experts within each layer and allocates slots by marginal covered demand. The resulting plan specifies both per-layer capacities and the IDs loaded into HBM and CPU. The runtime maintains a joint recency order across those tiers. A CPU hit promotes the selected expert and demotes the GPU LRU expert; a cold admission can also evict a host resident. A host mirror supplies the weights of each demoted GPU resident. Host admission reuses this copy through a metadata update. Stream tracking keeps tensor storage live through kernel execution. Serving requests update the profiled resident set within each layer's compiled capacity. The resulting cache state is reused across tokens and requests. Weight delivery follows the selected experts' read and copy dependencies before GPU execution. Prefill submits cold reads for the active expert batch, while decode loads selected experts on demand. The compiler and runtime address each weight block by its layer/expert ID. This key links profiled experts to placement, cache updates, and FP16~execution.
 
 This paper makes three contributions.
-\begin{list}{}{\setlength{\leftmargin}{16pt}\setlength{\labelwidth}{14pt}\setlength{\labelsep}{2pt}\setlength{\itemsep}{3pt}\setlength{\topsep}{3pt}}
+\begin{list}{}{\setlength{\leftmargin}{16pt}\setlength{\labelwidth}{14pt}\setlength{\labelsep}{2pt}\setlength{\itemsep}{9pt}\setlength{\topsep}{6pt}}
 \item[(1)] \textbf{Allocating capacity by layer.} We compile per-layer HBM/CPU capacities and initial expert IDs from routing profiles. Comparing each layer's next uncovered rank assigns shared slots to the demand they cover. Initialization loads the highest-ranked experts into HBM and the next ranks into CPU.
 \item[(2)] \textbf{Retaining experts after GPU eviction.} We maintain recency across HBM and CPU. A CPU promotion frees a host slot for the evicted GPU expert, preserving its weights for later reuse. Demotion reuses the host mirror through a metadata update.
 \item[(3)] \textbf{Adapting residency to serving requests.} We combine profile-based initialization with request-driven admission. Experts selected during serving enter the resident set and displace older entries within the compiled capacities. Residency persists across tokens and requests as the active expert set changes.
